{{!
  Klabis customization: a verbatim fork of the stock JavaSpring pathParams.mustache with ONE
  addition — the x-klabis-owner-id section below, which emits @OwnerId on the generated interface
  method's parameter.

  Rationale: @OwnerId names the parameter holding the owner's ID, so that @OwnerVisible on the
  operation has something to resolve ownership against. It used to reach the generator as
  x-field-extra-annotation, stamped on during bundling, which also forced the bundler to inline
  any shared $ref parameter so the annotation landed on one operation only. Reading the key here
  instead means the annotation can sit on the shared parameter: @OwnerId is inert on its own —
  both HasAuthorityMethodInterceptor.checkOwnership() and RequestBodyFieldAuthorizationAdvice
  only consult it for a method or field already marked @OwnerVisible.

  Maintenance: this is a vendor fork and nothing detects drift. On an openapi-generator upgrade,
  diff it against the new stock JavaSpring/pathParams.mustache and port the addition across.
}}
